{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/the-world-below/1523336-sell-me-on-world-below","id":1523336,"title":"Sell me on World Below","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Earthbane Cycle","The World Below"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-29T21:22:25-07:00","id":1523336,"title":"Sell me on World Below","content":"I'm great fan of <b>Storypath</b>. I bought at least corebook to any gameline till this day of it (even <b>Dystopia Rising</b>). I'm literally Admin of polish Storypath all games Facebook group and <b>They Came From</b> english one. But for <b>World Below</b> I cannot find hype in me.<br /> <br /> Maybe cause to me it sounds like 'generic postapo fantasy' to me? Maybe I miss some really storytelling shattering secret from Ashcan? Or it will simply be not my jive? ( However, I enjoy settings like <b>Dark Sun</b>. <b>Planescape</b> or even slightly <b>Dystopia Risin</b>g.) And I can find the same themes in <b>Realms of Pugmire</b>, with added 'animal humor' to it?<br /> <br /> So... Sell me on <b>World Below</b>! ( Best before crowdfunding of it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-30-2023, 07:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T00:59:41-07:00","id":1523342,"title":"","content":"Personally i have always correlated World Below far more with:<br /> <br /> - <b>Moria</b> and its fall in Middle Earth.<br /> - The <i><b>Dwarf Fortress</b></i> video game.<br /> - the D1-3 series of adventures for Greyhawk (plus <i>Queen of the Demonweb Pits</i>\u200b).<br /> - Randolph Carter's encounter with the ghouls and Gugs in Lovecraft's <i>Quest to Unknown Kadath</i>.<br /> - Clark Ashton Smith's morbidly comical <a href=\"http://eldritchdark.com/writings/short-stories/192/the-seven-geases\" target=\"_blank\">the Seven Geases</a>.<br /> - <a href=\"https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/william-hope-hodgson/the-house-on-the-borderland\" target=\"_blank\">the House on the Borderland</a> and <a href=\"https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/william-hope-hodgson/the-night-land\" target=\"_blank\">the Night Land</a> by William Hope Hodgson.<br /> - the claustrophobic jade ghost citadels from Conan short stories <a href=\"https://gutenberg.org/ebooks/32759\" target=\"_blank\">Red Nails</a> and <a href=\"http://gutenberg.net.au/ebooks06/0601051h.html\" target=\"_blank\">Xuthal of the Dusk</a>.<br /> <br /> - Or, much closer to home (in-house products) in the context of Exalted, the narrative of the Jadeborn and their sometimes embattled existence alongside the Endless Hordes of beings - primordial, created, mutated or cursed - exiled, imprisoned or escaped into the earthen depths in many different waves from the time when Primordials ruled existence on to the Age of Sorrows.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Postapo fantasy&quot; has always figured very low in my list of associations overall.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-30-2023, 04:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T08:36:22-07:00","id":1523354,"title":"","content":"Mechanically what interests me the most is the Kalm-phase that is this whole downtime-phase of the game where after you've returned from your adventures you deal with settlement-management and stuff like that. Matthew Dawkins compared it to Pendragon. Not a lot of fantasy-games where that part has a designated phase in the game. This is certainly what intrigues me the most.<br /> <br /> As for the setting... Hmm, since it's a completely new one I think I want to wait until I can read the actual book cover to cover before making up my mind about it. And personally, I like my settings weird and listening to the latest podcast about character-creation and that stuff about idols and stones being absorbed/recycled certainly sounds like the kind of weird I like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T23:00:27-07:00","id":1533681,"title":"","content":"<i><b>Mantis People</b></i> from <b>Monster's Ecology</b> coming book may convince me to look over this line again... \ud83d\ude0e ( Preview is at 12:00 of <a href=\"https://www.podbean.com/ea/pb-fmi92-15d2df4\" target=\"_blank\">this Pathcast</a> )<br /> <br /> I may even steal them to Realms of Pugmire games! \ud83d\ude31 ( In RoP we already have Giant Ants as Species in the world )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}